    <worksheet name='Target Distribution'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>Distribution of Heart Disease Cases</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='fkGroteskNeue,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Segoe UI,Roboto,Helvetica Neue,Arial,Noto Sans,sans-serif,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Noto Color Emoji,Hiragino Sans,PingFang SC,Apple SD Gothic Neo,Yu Gothic,Microsoft YaHei,Microsoft JhengHei,Meiryo' fontsize='16'> Pie chart showing the distribution of heart disease diagnosis in the UCI Heart Disease dataset. The chart reveals that 165 patients (54.5%) were diagnosed with heart disease (shown in blue), while 138 patients (45.5%) showed no signs of disease (shown in orange). This relatively balanced distribution makes the dataset suitable for predictive modeling without significant class imbalance issues. </run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
